    "text": "To determine how far Samuel is from the hotel, we need to calculate the distance he has traveled at each speed and then sum these distances.\n\nFirst, we calculate the distance Samuel travels at 50 miles per hour for 3 hours:\n\\[\n50 \\text{ miles/hour} \\times 3 \\text{ hours} = 150 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the distance Samuel travels at 80 miles per hour for 4 hours:\n\\[\n80 \\text{ miles/hour} \\times 4 \\text{ hours} = 320 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nNow, we add the two distances together to find the total distance Samuel has traveled:\n\\[\n150 \\text{ miles} + 320 \\text{ miles} = 470 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nSince Samuel started 600 miles from the hotel, the distance he is from the hotel is:\n\\[\n600 \\text{ miles} - 470 \\text{ miles} = 130 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{130}\n\\]",
